## Shared Web implementation checkpoint ΓÇö dynamic Strategy/School catalog

Shared Web has reconciled the current FCR-0128 selector semantics in the Web presentation path.

Preserved/implemented:
- catalog items remain externally supplied rather than hard-coded Falcon product truth;
- retired/replaced entries are not offered as current;
- `CATALOG_PRESENT + NOT_APPLICABLE_TO_CURRENT_ASSET -> VISIBLE_DISABLED_WITH_REASON` remains enforced by `catalogPresentation`;
- selector visibility does not create Strategy activation, Trading authority or entitlement;
- School/Strategy labels are localized at the Web surface without changing Application semantics.

Existing focused contract coverage remains in `tests/contracts.test.mjs`; composition/catalog rendering was reconciled during checkpoint 03.

Checkpoint record: `applications/shared/web/docs/FCR_RECONCILIATION_IMPLEMENTATION_CHECKPOINT_03.md` at commit `757c7d48fcda17b5b8dbfb886765fe71b1467273`.

No closure is claimed because governed executable Web verification and authoritative runtime catalog binding remain pending.

`HANDOFF_UPDATE_REQUIRED: Waiting On=WEB; Next Required Action=Complete governed executable verification of dynamic catalog visibility/applicability behavior and bind only through the governed Trading catalog projection when runtime transport becomes available.; Target Foundation Stage/WP=N/A ΓÇö APPLICATION/WEB CROSS-WORKSTREAM CONTRACT; Review Trigger=governed Web verification; material Trading catalog/applicability/entitlement change.`

APPLICATION CROSS-WORKSTREAM UPDATE ΓÇö 2026-08-16

FCR-0220 now records generic dynamic market-profile semantics for future advisory markets. It preserves the existing FCR-0128 catalog contracts and adds market context:
- dynamic market, never a hard-coded Saudi special case;
- Trading catalog remains authoritative;
- Strategy/School visible != activated;
- applicability can vary by market/asset;
- Saudi motivating mode: `ADVISORY_ONLY`, horizons Daily/Weekly/Monthly, no intraday/execution/follow-up.

No current FCR-0128 header change requested. FCR-0128 remains `Waiting On: WEB`.
